    "The audit retains only successfully parsed controls and complete supplied-member sets, including a successful feature-vector prefix after a later parse failure. Full configured target/features/ILP/DFG options expose all 6/56/7/3 stored fields and six real feature-vector presence flags.",
    "Actual selected EventDataView and cached source identities remain explicit. DFG precision preserves its original supplied bytes and native constructor defaults without cached selector overlay. Opt-in ILP accepts native integer limits; legacy requests keep their existing cap and parsing behavior.",
    "Complete native results remain successful when independent legacy presentation or optional source export fails. Actual legacy/source bytes, native exporter exceptions and transport display errors remain separate. Raw controls, original uploads, full native tables, reports, CSV and selected records can be inspected and downloaded.",
    "The existing prediction-target/feature transformation panels, ILP Miner and supplied-DFG precision section expose Exact native controls. Cancellation and source/replacement guards preserve actual request ownership. Compact portable fixtures retain every selected response and every physical request, including the malformed historical transport attempt."
  ],
